{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses took the blood and sprinkled it on the people.</b> He sprinkled the blood upon them so that they would enter into the covenant with the Holy One, blessed be He, in blood. And that bloodstain upon their garments Scripture called עדי (ornaments/testimony), because it was a testimony to them and great glory, and it was for them a testimony and a sign that they had entered into the covenant of the Holy One, blessed be He. Therefore, when they sinned with the calf and transgressed the covenant, He said to them (Exodus 33), ״הורד עדיך מעליך״ — 'remove your ornaments from upon you' — meaning that they should remove from themselves those garments that were עדי to them. And this is what is said (ibid.), ״ויתנצלו בני ישראל את עדים״ — 'and the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments' — those garments upon which the blood of the covenant had been sprinkled, which was a testimony and a sign between the Holy One, blessed be He, and them. And why did the Holy One, blessed be He, make a covenant with them in blood? It was a hint to them: if you fulfill the Torah, well and good; and if not, I permit your blood to be shed and to death. This is what our Rabbi Hananel, of blessed memory, wrote." "<b>And so</b> Rashi explained: he sprinkled from the blood upon their garments, and the matter was to give them importance, in the manner of what is written concerning Aaron (Exodus 29), ״והזית על אהרן ועל בגדיו ועל בניו ועל בגדי בניו״. And the intent of Onkelos, of blessed memory, when he said 'on the people,' is that he cast the blood upon the altar to make atonement for the people, for thus he translated: ואריק על מדבחא לכפרא על עמא — 'and I will cast upon the altar to make atonement for the people.'" "<b>There are those who</b> explained ויזרוק על העם — 'and he sprinkled on the people' — as כנגד העם, 'toward the people,' that is, before them, not upon their garments. And likewise (Genesis 1:20), ״ועוף יעופף על הארץ על פני רקיע השמים״ — 'and birds shall fly upon the earth across the face of the firmament of heaven' — whose meaning is 'toward the face of the firmament of heaven.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:35.386747290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}